🔥 This is the lesson I want you to absorb

Your first program assumed:

1 student = 1 valid score

Real-world data taught you:

Assumptions can be wrong.

That's one of the most important lessons in data science and AI.

Before training a model, you need to understand:

What does each column mean?
What values are missing?
What values are invalid?
What types are they?
Are there duplicates?
Are there outliers?
What assumptions are we making?

Garbage in → garbage out.